# NOTE THE `**` ON EVERY PATTERN. `.dockerignore` is NOT `.gitignore`: its patterns are matched
# against paths relative to the build context root, so a bare `.env` matches only a root-level
# `.env` and would NOT exclude `backend/.env`. Both files this really has to keep out of the image
# live one level down, so the prefix is load-bearing, not decoration.

# Credentials. `backend/.env` holds the service-role key. It is gitignored, so it cannot reach the
# Space through git — but a local `docker build` would copy it straight into the image.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# `COPY backend/ ./` would otherwise pull in `backend/.venv/` — a whole second Python install.
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.ruff_cache/

# Below this line is build SPEED, not image contents: `COPY backend/ ./` never copies these, but
# every excluded path is one the daemon no longer has to receive as build context. `node_modules/`
# alone is the bulk of the repo.
frontend/
data/
.git/
